{
  "_comment": "The GPU coding pool's model ladder, smallest first, signed into every release (engine/release.py coding_tiers) and read by the coordinator through engine/coding_ladder.py. min_vram_gb is the pooled VRAM a tier needs (the research estimate with headroom, see PROPOSAL.md 6.1, not the marketing size); context is the total engine context the tier is meant to run with. A tier is used only while enabled is true; blocked says why one is held back and must be cleared before it is enabled. Each file comes from a pinned Hugging Face revision with its exact size and SHA-256. A model published in parts lists them under files, in order (llama.cpp loads part 1 and finds the rest by name).",
  "_sources": "Research 2026-10-25 (/tmp/claude-1000/model-ladder/PROPOSAL.md and models.proposed.json): revisions, sizes and hashes read from the Hugging Face API at the pinned commit. The 16 GB tier is the file live on TheWall since 2026-10-25 (same entry as scripts/app_models.json qwen36-a3b). Owner approved the 24, 32 and 48 GB tiers on 2026-10-25.",
  "_placeholders": "The 64 GB and larger tiers are placeholders, not decisions: Qwen3.8 Flash-Next is under the Qwen Community License 1.0, whose commercial clause needs the owner's decision, the owner wants other heavyweight (1M-context) models researched first, and the coordinator's model download cannot fetch a model in parts yet. Replace or remove them freely.",
